{
  "slug": "sdlc-kit",
  "name": "Sdlc Kit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Spec-Driven Development for Claude Code. 11 skills for the daily PR loop — init, PRDs, ADRs, SDD specs (EARS), tasks, git worktrees, code reviews (Code Reviewer + AppSec dual-axis), retrospectives. Includes a PostToolUse hook that auto-indexes every .md save into a SQLite tracker. Self-contained HTML dashboard (Kanban + branch graph) included.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **11 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (11): `sdlc-adr` (Use when the user wants to record, review, or transition an Architecture Decision Record (ADR) — one file…), `sdlc-dash` (Use when the user wants to open the SDLC Kit vault dashboard in their default browser — a…), `sdlc-init` (Use when the user wants to initialize an SDLC (Spec-Driven Development) vault in a Git project), `sdlc-prd` (Use when the user wants to create, review, or transition a Product Requirements Document (PRD) — the top-level…), `sdlc-retro` (Use when the user wants to hold, facilitate, or close out a sprint / iteration retrospective — the…), `sdlc-review` (Use when the user wants to record, finalize, or transition a code-review record for a Pull Request —…), `sdlc-spec` (Use when the user wants to create or mature a Spec-Driven Development (SDD) trio — `requirements.md` (EARS notation,…), `sdlc-status` (Use at the start of any session or when the user asks for a quick health check of…), and 3 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install sdlc-kit@claude-community` from `vellus-ai/sdlc-kit` (`plugins/core`).",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "skill",
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "Vellus",
    "url": "https://vellus.tech/"
  },
